00:27:49.461 --> 00:27:50.320
or to your business?

00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:51.711
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:27:51.711 --> 00:27:53.470
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:27:53.470 --> 00:27:55.159
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to the guys

00:27:55.159 --> 00:27:56.091
from VNR Media.

00:27:56.091 --> 00:27:58.437
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:27:58.437 --> 00:28:01.118
Your One Word, and for the
fun interview that we did

00:28:01.118 --> 00:28:03.428
on your channel, it was
a blast and I'm excited

00:28:03.428 --> 00:28:05.279
to see where your channel goes, guys.

00:28:05.279 --> 00:28:08.090
- Our guest today is
Evan Carmichael and Evan,

00:28:08.090 --> 00:28:11.180
he was recognized by Forbes
as one of the worlds top

00:28:11.180 --> 00:28:13.451
40 social marketing talents.

00:28:13.451 --> 00:28:16.183
Ink Magazine rated him as
one of the top 25 social

00:28:16.183 --> 00:28:18.102
media keynote speakers you need to know.

00:28:18.102 --> 00:28:21.784
And he had recently published
a book called Your One Word.

00:28:21.784 --> 00:28:23.373
- So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:28:23.373 --> 00:28:26.371
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:28:26.371 --> 00:28:28.470
and whatever your one word is.

00:28:28.470 --> 00:28:31.442
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:28:31.442 --> 00:28:34.859
(dramatic deep drumming)

00:28:36.789 --> 00:28:40.880
- I have a pad of post it
notes, yes, post it notes,

00:28:40.880 --> 00:28:43.880
next to my sink in my bathroom, why?

00:28:45.393 --> 00:28:48.001
Well, because after I brush my teeth,

00:28:48.001 --> 00:28:49.190
I haven't looked at my phone yet,

00:28:49.190 --> 00:28:53.352
I take a post it note out
and I write the three things

00:28:53.352 --> 00:28:55.411
I need to focus on today.

00:28:55.411 --> 00:28:58.446
And then you know what I do with it?

00:28:58.446 --> 00:29:00.429
I stick it on the back of my phone.

00:29:00.429 --> 00:29:01.897
Now why would I do that?

00:29:01.897 --> 00:29:03.685
Because I have my phone
with me all the time.

00:29:03.685 --> 00:29:05.685
So if it's on the back of my phone,

00:29:05.685 --> 00:29:08.720
I'm going to get a visual
cue to remind me and

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:12.651
keep it top of mind so
I stay focused on it.

00:29:12.651 --> 00:29:15.744
How is it that you see
something larger for yourself?

00:29:15.744 --> 00:29:17.364
Well, the first thing that you have to do,

00:29:17.364 --> 00:29:21.531
the very first thing, is you
have to get out of the weeds.

00:29:23.503 --> 00:29:26.931
Success for people are all in the weeds.

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:30.189
The busier you are, the
more you have going on.

00:29:30.189 --> 00:29:31.578
You know that old saying
that everybody says,

00:29:31.578 --> 00:29:34.979
don't work in your business,
work on your business.

00:29:34.979 --> 00:29:37.329
But we're all in the weeds.

00:29:37.329 --> 00:29:40.588
And the key to seeing
something larger for yourself

00:29:40.588 --> 00:29:42.648
is getting out of the weeds.

00:29:42.648 --> 00:29:46.156
And don't you feel like this dude?

00:29:46.156 --> 00:29:50.868
I know I do, (mumbles)
wake up, brush your teeth,

00:29:50.868 --> 00:29:55.625
make the coffee, feed the
kids, pack the lunches,

00:29:55.625 --> 00:29:57.895
put them on the bus, get in the car,

00:29:57.895 --> 00:30:02.030
text your friends, get some
coffee, arrive at work,

00:30:02.030 --> 00:30:05.760
feign interest, answer
emails, update Facebook,

00:30:05.760 --> 00:30:09.848
make cold calls, avoid
the meeting, look busy,

00:30:09.848 --> 00:30:13.659
crunch some numbers, update
Facebook, get in the car,

00:30:13.659 --> 00:30:17.801
go to carpool, feed
your kids, feed the dog,

00:30:17.801 --> 00:30:21.456
check email, update
Facebook, kiss your husband,

00:30:21.456 --> 00:30:24.547
climb into bed, fool
around, are you kidding?

00:30:24.547 --> 00:30:27.318
I'm exhausted, turn off the lights.

00:30:27.318 --> 00:30:28.724
(audience laughing)

00:30:28.724 --> 00:30:31.699
I mean, I live in a two household...

00:30:31.699 --> 00:30:32.787
Thank you.

00:30:32.787 --> 00:30:36.787
Entrepreneurial family,
I'm exhausted, I'm busy.

00:30:38.308 --> 00:30:40.027
How the heck am I going
to see something larger

00:30:40.027 --> 00:30:42.805
for my life when I have a business to run,

00:30:42.805 --> 00:30:44.496
when I have kids to take care of?

00:30:44.496 --> 00:30:47.336
Well, you have to get out of the weeds.

00:30:47.336 --> 00:30:49.464
And the truth is there's some good news,

00:30:49.464 --> 00:30:52.134
and the goods news is I
heard that this pill that's

00:30:52.134 --> 00:30:52.967
in development.

00:30:52.967 --> 00:30:55.800
(people laughing)

00:30:56.764 --> 00:31:00.523
Well, I know, I'm waiting for it too.

00:31:00.523 --> 00:31:02.914
And you know, the problem
though is I think they're

00:31:02.914 --> 00:31:06.176
going to have naming problems,
Forgetitol seems like

00:31:06.176 --> 00:31:09.055
a bad name for a pill,
even though I might take it

00:31:09.055 --> 00:31:11.444
now and again, so I thought
before we jump into how

00:31:11.444 --> 00:31:13.454
you see something larger,
I need to yank you out

00:31:13.454 --> 00:31:14.389
of the weeds first.

00:31:14.389 --> 00:31:17.613
So I'm going to give you
my advice for what I do

00:31:17.613 --> 00:31:20.281
in order to keep myself out of the weeds,

00:31:20.281 --> 00:31:22.313
and you guys don't need
remedial personal development,

00:31:22.313 --> 00:31:25.110
I got that, I just feel
obligated to give you some

00:31:25.110 --> 00:31:27.501
actionable things to do
because if you don't plan

00:31:27.501 --> 00:31:31.366
your week out before the week starts,

00:31:31.366 --> 00:31:32.820
you're going to be in reactive mode.

00:31:32.820 --> 00:31:33.811
You're going to be running around,

00:31:33.811 --> 00:31:36.931
you're going to be chasing
down the biggest thing

00:31:36.931 --> 00:31:38.432
that's happening in your life.

00:31:38.432 --> 00:31:41.014
You're going to be constantly responding.

00:31:41.014 --> 00:31:42.873
This is one of the most
important things that you can do,

00:31:42.873 --> 00:31:45.442
if you're not married, if
you're not living with somebody,

00:31:45.442 --> 00:31:49.080
do it for yourself, plan your
week, you know this all ready.

00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:52.060
The first thing that you
need to do is you define

00:31:52.060 --> 00:31:54.070
what success looks like for
you, and it's not 10 million

00:31:54.070 --> 00:31:55.768
dollars in the bank, I'm sorry.

00:31:55.768 --> 00:31:58.499
It needs to be something
bigger, a bigger--

00:31:58.499 --> 00:32:00.008
- What if somebody says
it is 10 million dollars

00:32:00.008 --> 00:32:00.888
in the bank to me?

00:32:00.888 --> 00:32:02.578
- Well, you know, I mean,
the problem with saying it's

00:32:02.578 --> 00:32:06.069
10 million dollars in the
bank is that when you finally

00:32:06.069 --> 00:32:08.947
get to the 10 million dollars,
typically those people

00:32:08.947 --> 00:32:10.028
feel pretty bankrupt because--

00:32:10.028 --> 00:32:11.447
- And that's what you're
saying your (mumbles).

00:32:11.447 --> 00:32:13.050
- Absolutely, absolutely.

00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:15.087
And so, once you define it for yourself,

00:32:15.087 --> 00:32:18.277
I think the key is how do you
then trick yourself, Donnie,

00:32:18.277 --> 00:32:21.249
into feeling successful every single day?

00:32:21.249 --> 00:32:24.257
I got a daughter that plays
lacrosse, she's nine years old.

00:32:24.257 --> 00:32:26.876
If I said to her, I'm only
cheering for you when you

00:32:26.876 --> 00:32:30.105
score a goal, how do you think
she'd feel during the game?

00:32:30.105 --> 00:32:32.057
She wouldn't play very
well, that's for sure.

00:32:32.057 --> 00:32:35.034
So you've got to figure out
how do you cheer for yourself,

00:32:35.034 --> 00:32:37.532
and how do you feel successful
while you're playing

00:32:37.532 --> 00:32:39.398
the game, because it's
not all about the goal.

00:32:39.398 --> 00:32:41.128
- Are there any tools that
you want to share with us?

00:32:41.128 --> 00:32:41.961
Give me a...

00:32:41.961 --> 00:32:43.920
Today I want to feel
better inside, I'm at home,

00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:46.770
I'm watching, I'm either
somebody that's got the millions

00:32:46.770 --> 00:32:48.029
of dollars and is not feeling good,

00:32:48.029 --> 00:32:50.540
or I don't have those
millions of dollars and

00:32:50.540 --> 00:32:52.868
it's not feeling good, worrying
about the economy around me,

00:32:52.868 --> 00:32:54.491
so give me (mumbles) session.

00:32:54.491 --> 00:32:56.310
- Exactly what you need to
do, what you need to do is

00:32:56.310 --> 00:32:58.168
you have to decide, okay,
this is where I'm going,

00:32:58.168 --> 00:33:00.130
I'm going for the big
vision of what success is.

00:33:00.130 --> 00:33:03.070
Now, do a head fake with
yourself and say, okay,

00:33:03.070 --> 00:33:05.131
let's just say that I'm
actually all ready there,

00:33:05.131 --> 00:33:06.878
I have the 10 million dollars in the bank,

00:33:06.878 --> 00:33:09.769
I'm saving the world, whatever
it is that your version

00:33:09.769 --> 00:33:12.754
of success is, what are three
things that I would change

00:33:12.754 --> 00:33:16.221
about this day, today,
how would I live it today,

00:33:16.221 --> 00:33:17.693
if I all ready had that stuff?

00:33:17.693 --> 00:33:18.683
What time would I wake up?

00:33:18.683 --> 00:33:19.974
Who's my first phone call to?

00:33:19.974 --> 00:33:21.122
What did I eat for breakfast?

00:33:21.122 --> 00:33:24.806
Start living as that success vision now.

00:33:24.806 --> 00:33:25.852
(soft drumming)

